  "kind": "Bounded reference and import models with separately reviewed concrete guard mappings.",
  "correspondence": "Two Libraries with overlapping Skill IDs and paths; immutable manifest selection separated from current lookup; two imported objects and one bounded create outcome per object. Resource identity is an authority union, not a required Notion File row.",
  "review_basis": "Reviewed the approved single-track contract and the named source guards, their behavior assertions, and relevant callers on the task overlay based on ffe3b0255bea1d5a12a62c3832ec7f7175c27dd1. Fixed selection is checked against exact owner, manifest and path; Source resolution keeps original repository authority. Import guard correspondence includes creation-only inferred Members, explicit empty values, frozen operation progress and read-only completion recovery. Shared never-replay operation evidence uses an unknown append; public batch tests separately cover unknown CREATE. SQLite codec and cross-process persistence are concrete preservation obligations outside the TLA state variables. The initial 23-case design-model run and the 4 new selected-reference regression cases were observed separately; this source mapping is not a declaration that actual mutations, final model bytes, packed artifacts or live Notion passed. The official format pass changed layout only; named mutation anchors were rechecked against the formatted source. Final review removes the unreachable name/catalog fallback after exact entry binding and retains the same denial invalidation. The contract now uses the actual positional ctl library inspect ENTRY syntax; database aliases remain entry conveniences, not portable Library IDs.",
