      "scope": "Current exact Skill ID lookup rejects multiple physical claims rather than choosing the first. Source membership and complete pagination remain separate reader obligations."
    },
    {
      "name": "immutable_selected_reference",
      "files": [
        "packages/core/src/snapshot.ts",
        "packages/core/test/skill-reference-guards.test.ts",
        "packages/core/test/shared-current-relative.test.ts"
      ],
      "scope": "The selected manifest must own the complete Library/Skill key. Missing pin cannot be discarded for current. A pathless pin uses its manifest entrypoint despite a changed current kind; a missing path cannot be repaired. Cross-owner references do not inherit the containing snapshot."
    },
    {
      "name": "source_coordinate_authority",
      "files": [
        "packages/core/src/shared-source-references.ts",
        "packages/core/test/shared-source-references.test.ts"
      ],
      "scope": "Original Source revision/path wins over a coincidentally mounted local path. Frozen Source route plus bytes is sufficient without a Notion File row; repository provenance and complete inventory are assumed by the finite model."
    },
    {
      "name": "member_input_tristate",
      "files": [
        "packages/core/src/shared-current-member-discovery.ts",
        "packages/core/test/shared-current-member-discovery.test.ts",
        "packages/cli/test/current-members.test.ts"
      ],
      "scope": "Existing omitted Members are preserved, explicit empty wins, and first-creation inference cannot populate Requires. Exact links prove identity, not natural-language intent."
    },
    {
      "name": "frozen_import_recovery",
      "files": [
        "packages/core/src/shared-current-import-plan-model.ts",
        "packages/core/src/shared-current-write.ts",
        "packages/core/test/shared-current-import-plan.test.ts"
      ],
      "scope": "Completed steps cannot regress or change request identity. A completed frozen import resumes by exact readback without recompiling or replaying its body phase. Arbitrary batches and durable crash boundaries remain concrete tests."
    },
    {
      "name": "unobserved_nonidempotent_action",
      "files": [
        "packages/core/src/shared-current-operation.ts",
        "packages/core/test/shared-current-operation.test.ts"
      ],
      "scope": "A previously dispatched never-replay action cannot be resent because fresh observation is empty. The common kernel assertion is exercised with an unknown append; CREATE-specific behavior is separately covered by public import-batch regressions."
    },
    {
      "name": "persisted_complete_identity",
      "files": [
        "packages/core/src/cache-address.ts",
        "packages/core/test/sqlite-state.node.test.ts"
      ],
      "scope": "Storage segments decode to the full logical identity. Separate real Node processes persist two Libraries with the same scope, stable ID and version, then retire one while preserving the other and its publication fence. Physical storage and SQL are not modeled TLA variables."
    }
  ],
  "unmodeled_bindings": [
    {
      "kind": "concrete_regressions",
      "scope": "URI parser bytes/encoding/case, exact physical Notion membership, permissions and denied scopes, complete pagination, native/resource/Source bytes and modes, current acquisition fences, arbitrary batches, external Notion concurrency, CLI crash/SQLite durability, packaged SDK/Broker and live-model delivery require concrete evidence."
    },
    {
      "kind": "relationship_semantics",
      "scope": "Members means optional discoverable members. Exact active links establish target identity, not arbitrary author intent. Requires is explicit. Cross-Library relationship federation is not supported."
    },
    {
      "kind": "stable_identity_lifetime",
      "scope": "Authors must not reuse a deleted stable ID for a different Skill. The current implementation has no permanent global tombstone registry; the finite model does not prove identity ownership across deletion and reuse."
    }
  ],
